  "fresh ethanol 1.0 mol/s at 16.2 bar / 30 C (stated boundary conditions); feed ethanol anhydrous",
  "hydrogen recycle to the superheater starts as 0.3 mol/s (document: hydrogen-rich gas from knockout pot 26, compressed to 15.5 bar); the closed loop sets its real value",
  "superheater outlet pressure 14.8 bar is stated; here the pressure follows the feed (16.2 bar) minus 0.35 bar per reactor so reactor 22 leaves at about 14.8 bar",
  "reheaters 12, 16 (figure only) and 20 bring the gas back to 235 C, the stated reactor 10 inlet temperature; each bed leaves at 212.5 C, the stated reactor 10 exit window 205-220 C (the beds are adiabatic in the patent; with DWSIM's NRTL enthalpies an adiabatic equilibrium bed warmed up instead, so the stated exit temperature is imposed and the duty the engine then reports is a measure of that inconsistency)",
  "gas split: 20 % recycled to compressor 29, 75 % purged (hydrogen is the co-product), 5 % to compressor 35 (not stated)",
  "hydrogenation reactor 38 adiabatic at the mixed-feed pressure; acetaldehyde fully hydrogenated",
  "the dissolved hydrogen is removed completely ahead of column 40 (condenser 48 purge, line 49) as a specified split: a trace of hydrogen in the total condenser pushed the column's top temperature to 4 C",
  "column 40: 20 stages, total condenser (the hydrogen leaves in the knock-out ahead of it as the line-49 purge), feed stage 10, top 1.5 bar (stated), 0.1 bar drop; the ester/ethanol azeotrope is taken as the liquid distillate and sent to column 52 (the patent's side draw 51); the side draw itself is not drawn",
  "column 40 bottoms draw = feed - 1.3 x the ester fed; reboiler 43 is the column's own reboiler",
  "column 52: 20 stages, total condenser, feed stage 10, top 12 bar (stated), 0.2 bar drop; bottoms draw from the azeotrope balance below (the stated product is 'substantially pure ethyl acetate')",
  "column 52 bottoms draw 0.0990 mol/s from the ester balance with a 28 mol% ester azeotrope overhead at 12 bar",
  "water removal package 46: 99 % of the water removed, specified not simulated"
